window.products.push({"id":428881,"name":"Royal Albert 100 Years of Royal Albert Set, Poppy, 3-Piece","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":107.65,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/91gq8yU4DSL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Product Description Royal Doulton announces the international launch of the 100 Years of Royal Albert collection, celebrating a century of English craftsmanship through ten patterns representing design trends of each decade of the 20th century. Royal Albert’s success dates back to the late 1800’s, and the new collection celebrates the brand’s vitality, longevity and rich design history. The collection features all bone china with 22 karat gold accents on teacups, saucers, plates, mugs, teapots, creamers, sugar bowls and figurines. Every pattern included in the collection captures the true historical design statements and trends of each time period. Featuring Royal Albert brand signature delicate florals in many of the patterns, all items from the 100 Years of Royal Albert collection are packaged in unique deep pink and burgundy Royal Albert hatboxes with illustrations of all ten patterns. 1970 Poppy: reflecting the decade’s ‘flower power’ spirit with bright coral orange and yellow colors. Amazon.com As it embarks on a new century of fine china design, Royal Albert honors the artistic achievements of the one it has so faithfully chronicled with this stunning 100 Years of Royal Albert tribute collection. Employing classic shapes and delicate floral motifs, the 10-part series, which includes teaware, figurines, and brooches, recalls major British historical events and style trends from each decade of the 21st century. Inspiration for the series came from previous Royal Albert designs and its archive pattern books. The collection's 10 three-piece sets are a wonderfully social way to tell the entire story, and this 1970 \"Poppy\" makes a lovely chapter. Crafted of bone china with luxurious 22-karat gold trim on gracefully scalloped shapes, the teacup, saucer, and dessert plate represent the unforgettable era that included exciting space exploration and revolutionary social activism. Poppies--with their vivid coral orange and yellow hues--were extremely popular, and this design features trails of large blossoms with leafy green accents winding their way across a pristine white backdrop. Each piece has a special commemorative backstamp, and the set comes packaged in a presentation-style pink and burgundy hatbox with depictions of all the patterns. The china is dishwasher-safe and carries a two-year warranty. --Kara Karll","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/91gq8yU4DSL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Royal Albert","source_asin":"B0014TE0X4","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-428881","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0014TE0X4","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B0014TE0X4","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
